 Here's an example of a JavaScript function that uses the `incoming-webhook` package to send a message to a specified Slack channel with the given text:

First, you need to install the incoming-webhook package by running `npm install --save incoming-webhook` or `yarn add incoming-webhook`.

```javascript
const IncomingWebhook = require('incoming-webhook');

async function postMessageToSlack(text, channel) {
  try {
    const webhook = new IncomingWebhook(process.env.SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL); // Replace this with your actual webhook URL

    const options = {
      channel: channel,
      text: text,
    };

    await webhook.send(options);
    console.log(`Message sent to ${channel}: ${text}`);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(`Error sending message to Slack: ${error}`);
  }
}
```

Replace `process.env.SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` with your actual Slack webhook URL.

